[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "King's Gambit Accepted"]
[Variation "King's Gambit Accepted: Kieseritzky Gambit, Berlin Defense"]
[ECO "C39"]
[Character "gambit,sharp"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "both"]
[Tricks "trap"]
[Themes "open-f-file,centre-pawns"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "main"]
[Opponent "2...exf4 3.Nf3 g5"]
[Start "1. e4 e5 2. f4 exf4 3. Nf3"]

3... g5 { Black holds on to the extra pawn by guarding f4 with the g-pawn. This is the most common reply. } 4. h4 { Attacks the g5 pawn. If it is traded or driven off, nothing guards f4 and White gets the pawn back with a strong bishop. } 4... g4 5. Ne5 { The knight must move because the g4 pawn attacks it. On e5 it hits g4 and f7, and Black's d-pawn can only chase it after another move. } 5... Nf6 ( 5... d6 6. Nxg4 { Takes the g4 pawn, so White has the pawn back. If the bishop takes the knight, the queen takes the bishop. } 6... Nc6 7. Nc3 { Develops and prepares d4 and Bxf4. } ) 6. d4 { Builds a centre and opens the bishop on c1 so it can take the pawn on f4. } 6... d6 ( 6... d5 7. Bxf4 { Takes the pawn back with the bishop aimed at b8. } 7... Nh5 8. Bg5 { Attacks the queen on d8, so Black has to spend a move on it while its knight is stuck on h5. } ) 7. Nd3 { The black pawn attacked the knight, so it retreats with a threat to take on f4. } 7... Nxe4 8. Bxf4 { White has the pawn back. The bishop is active and Black's g4 pawn is cut off from help. } 8... Bg7 ( 8... Qe7 9. Be2 { Develops and blocks the e-file, so Black's queen has no check on the king. } 9... Nc6 10. Nc3 { Trades or drives off the strong knight on e4. } ) 9. Nc3 { Attacks the knight on e4. If it stays, Nxe4 wins it, so Black has to trade. } 9... Nxc3 10. bxc3 { Retakes towards the centre and keeps the d4 pawn guarded. It also opens the b-file for a rook. } 10... O-O 11. Be2 { Develops and aims at g4, the advanced pawn that is hard for Black to hold. Plan: win the g4 pawn, castle, and use the open f-file. The engine rates Black about a pawn better, which is the price of the gambit. If Black leaves the book, develop and take the centre before attacking. } 11... f5 *
